## Why This Is Asked

Backpressure in streaming pipelines is a common real-world pain point; this question probes ability to model skew, test end-to-end latency, and reason about autoscaling and resilience under bursts.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure, end-to-end latency, tail latency
- Autoscaling of Kafka, Spark, and storage
- Throughput under burst, circuit breakers, graceful degradation

## Code Example

```javascript
function percentile(arr, p) {
  if (!Array.isArray(arr) || arr.length === 0) return 0;
  const sorted = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.ceil(p/100 * sorted.length) - 1;
  return sorted[Math.max(0, Math.min(idx, sorted.length-1))];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you instrument latency tracking across components?
- How would you simulate bursty workloads without real traffic?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge caching behavior, tail latency, and backpressure under regional surge—a practical beginner scenario for performance testing.

## Key Concepts
- Edge caching and cache warming
- Tail latency (p95/p99)
- API gateway backpressure and circuit breakers
- Regional autoscaling and cost/latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = {
  scenarios: {
    regionalSurge: { executor: 'ramping-vus', startVUs: 0, stages: [ { duration: '2m', target: 50 }, { duration: '8m', target: 200 } ] }
  }
};
export default function () {
  http.get('https://region-A.example.com/pricing');
  http.post('https://region-A.example.com/book', JSON.stringify({}), { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  sleep(0.5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would network jitter influence your test results and how would you compensate for it?
- What signals would you use to decide if the edge cache warming was successful?

